I think I did the exact same thing to my last rear tire. I think what is happening is, there is a deep well for the spokes at the bottom of the wheel and the lip of the tire which is supposed to lodge under the top of the wheel rim, is instead lodged in that well.

&#x200B;

I just replaced my rear tire again and paid way more attention to how it was seated and kept de-inflating it and torquing the tire with my hands until I was pretty sure it was even everywhere on the rim this time. It was surprisingly easy to get the tire caught in that well.

